# Git attributes -- minimal binary pinning only.
#
# This file intentionally does NOT set `* text=auto eol=lf`. The repo's
# tracked files are currently mixed-eol (mostly CRLF on Windows-touched
# files, LF elsewhere); enabling text=auto would force a one-time
# renormalization that touches thousands of files and produces a giant
# auto-commit -- exactly the "symmetric ins/del" churn the hygiene pass
# was meant to prevent.
#
# To actually pin EOL to LF across the tree, do it in a dedicated commit:
#   1) extend this file with `* text=auto eol=lf` plus per-extension rules
#      (PowerShell / batch keep CRLF, shell scripts and source pin LF).
#   2) Run `git add --renormalize .` to re-stage every text file with
#      the new normalization.
#   3) Commit the result as a stand-alone "Apply LF normalization" change
#      so reviewers can see it isolated from real edits.
# Until then, the binary rules below stop git from accidentally trying to
# diff or auto-normalize the file types that should never be touched.

# Binary file types -- never line-ending normalized, never diffed.
*.exe      binary
*.dll      binary
*.lib      binary
*.a        binary
*.o        binary
*.obj      binary
*.so       binary
*.dylib    binary
*.pdb      binary
*.png      binary
*.jpg      binary
*.jpeg     binary
*.gif      binary
*.bmp      binary
*.ico      binary
*.icns     binary
*.tga      binary
*.dds      binary
*.wav      binary
*.mp3      binary
*.ogg      binary
*.ttf      binary
*.otf      binary
*.woff     binary
*.woff2    binary
*.bin      binary
*.dat      binary
*.z64      binary
*.n64      binary
*.v64      binary
*.seg      binary
*.ctl      binary
*.tbl      binary
*.docx     binary
*.xlsx     binary
*.pptx     binary
*.pdf      binary
*.zip      binary
*.7z       binary
*.tar      binary
*.gz       binary
*.bz2      binary
